###  http://data.europa.eu/949/linesideDistanceIndication
:linesideDistanceIndication rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:subPropertyOf :trackGenericObjParameter ;
                            rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                        :RunningTrack
                                                      )
                                        ] ;
                            rdfs:range :LinesideDistanceIndication ;
                            :formatNote """[NNNN] frequency in meters
Appearance - selectable list
[L/R] - the side along the track where the lineside indication is positioned (left or right)"""@en ;
                            :rinfIndex "1.1.1.0.0.3" ;
                            :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LinesideDistanceIndication> ;
                            :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.1.3" ;
                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-12-12"^^xsd:date ;
                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-01-30"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                "2025-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
                            rdfs:comment "Indication of types of appearance of track lineside distance indications."@en ;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                            rdfs:label "Lineside distance indication"@en ;
                            <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Frequency, appearance and positioning of a sign indicating distance as reference post. Two types of sign are normally available: kilometer post and hectometer post.
- A kilometer post is a lineside sign indicating the distance from a specific point, usually being the strarting point of the railway line.
- An hectometer post is a lineside sign indicating a relative distance."""@en .


